From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 03:36:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998-google-taimen: enable the video
 codec

Everything venus needs is now in place: msm8998.dtsi describes the block with
its clocks, GDSC, interrupt, IOMMU streams and bus votes, and
firmware-google-taimen ships qcom/venus-4.4/venus.mbn -- the exact name
msm8998_res asks for. Enabling it is the last line.

Enabled on the board rather than in the SoC dtsi: the node is only usable where
that firmware is installed, and no other msm8998 board in tree packages it.

This does NOT mean venus works. Loading venus_core still wedges the fabric
below printk. The node is enabled so the bring-up can be bisected with
venus_core's stop_at parameter on real hardware, and it is safe to carry ONLY
because the module is blacklisted from autoload -- see the comment in the DTS.
Booting this without that blacklist is a bootloop that needs a physical
Power+VolDown to escape.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts   | 28 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts
index 8fb5e1239fae..78b35ca9053a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts
@@ -1224,3 +1224,31 @@ imx179_ep: endpoint {
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Hardware video codec. The firmware is packaged -- firmware-google-taimen
+ * ships qcom/venus-4.4/venus.mbn, which is the name msm8998_res asks for --
+ * and msm8998.dtsi describes the block fully, so this is the last line needed
+ * to reach it.
+ *
+ * Enabled here, on the board, rather than in the SoC dtsi: the node is only
+ * usable where that firmware is actually installed, and no other msm8998 board
+ * in tree packages it.
+ *
+ * READ THIS BEFORE BOOTING WITHOUT A BLACKLIST. Loading venus_core kills the
+ * SoC below the level printk can reach -- a NoC timeout, no oops, no SMMU
+ * fault, recovered only by the hardware watchdog. Left to autoload that is a
+ * bootloop, and the bootloader does not fall back on its own: five reboots
+ * from the initramfs did not exhaust the A/B retry counter, and the way out is
+ * a physical Power+VolDown into fastboot. Keep venus_core, venus_dec and
+ * venus_enc blacklisted (/etc/modprobe.d/00-venus-bringup.conf, and
+ * modprobe.blacklist= on the cmdline) so the module is loaded by hand and a
+ * wedge costs one watchdog reset instead of the phone.
+ *
+ * venus_core's stop_at parameter bisects that wedge by declining to execute
+ * rather than by printing, which is the only kind of instrument that survives
+ * an unresponsive fabric.
+ */
+&venus {
+	status = "okay";
+};
